From 2e656801407c86c7f9ef6a00b0123cb3bf9f8235 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:55:17 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/15] Round 10: Let the calling thread evaluate in worker
 batches

A multi-worker batch now spawns min(workers, candidates) - 1 scoped
threads and runs the same claim loop on the calling thread, so the
number of concurrent evaluators is unchanged and one thread start and
join disappears. A test checks order, single evaluation per index and
the bound on distinct evaluating threads.

Workload: parallel (96 full records, 4 workers on 2 vCPUs), 11 samples.
Before median: 0.215 ms. After median: 0.183 ms. Speedup: 1.18x.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
